      (text "1. Noir Journalism – Shadowy Deals, Spin Doctors & Media Manipulation\n\"A Story Too Clean to Be True—When PR Erases the Bloodstains\"\n\n\"The Press Release That Killed a Scandal—And Built a Myth\"\n\n\"Who Owns the Truth? The Men in Power vs. The Reporters in the Dark\"\n\n\"Smoke, Lies & Headlines—How the Game of Public Image Is Won\"\n\n\"The Column That Should Have Burned—Journalism in the Grip of Influence\"\n\n\"Spokesmen, Fixers & Shadow Players—The Underbelly of Public Relations\"\n\n\"How a News Story Disappears Overnight—The Art of Making Controversy Vanish\"\n\n\"The Old Hacks Knew Better—Why No One Trusts Political Journalism Anymore\"\n\n> Stylistic Edge: Gritty, cynical, dripping with power plays and media deception, built on the murky ethics of PR spin.\n\n2. Dystopian Journalism – State-Controlled Messaging, Propaganda & Forbidden Narratives\n\"The Ministry of Communication Approves Your Statement—No Further Questions\"\n\n\"Today's Approved News—Unauthorised Stories W...")
