      (text "Photographs/footage \n\n3.3	Whilst the media often publish photographs taken from social media, careful thought should be given as to whether this is appropriate and/or justified in the case of photographs of the deceased or other victims.  In particular:\n(a)            The publication of such photographs may exacerbate the distress to Victims and/or families of the deceased.\n(b)            The publication of photographs may be an infringement of copyright (the copyright is usually owned by whoever took the photograph).\n(c)             It may also amount to an invasion of privacy and/or the data protection rights of those depicted in the photographs.\n(d)            In light of the highly distressing context of a terror attack, consideration should be given as to whether permission has been obtained/should be obtained prior to publishing a photograph\n3.4	The media should be mindful that the publication of a photograph of a person in a public place may amount to an unlawful invasion...")
      (truncated #t))
