      (text "SOC recommends the following motion is out of order being contrary to Rule 9(a)(ii), no instruction.  This DM notes the importance of Europe’s main human rights treaty, the European Convention on Human Rights, in protecting freedom of expression and freedom of the press.  It welcomes the EU’s recent, historic progress toward joining the European Convention on Human Rights and the ongoing work of the NUJ in protecting civil, political, social and economic rights of its members and more generally.  This DM notes that several lawmakers in the UK, a founding member of the Council of Europe, have expressed a desire for the UK to exit the convention. It equally notes that whilst there has been a change of government in the UK, the threat to the UK’s membership of the Council of Europe and the application of the European Convention of Human Rights remains.  Brussels Branch  SOC recommends that the following amendment puts motion 131 in order.  Insert at the end: “This DM instructs the NEC to ...")
