      (text "128 SOC recommends the following motion is out of order being contrary to Rule 9(a)(ii), no instruction.  This DM recognises that many people accuse journalists of being biased and unreliable. This can create a climate where misinformation, propaganda and conspiracy theories are seen as equally valid with well researched and ethical journalism.  The DM reaffirms that a functioning democracy needs accurate, dedicated journalism that is trusted by its citizens.  DM calls on the NEC to work with the Ethics Council to detail and promote the ethical basis of trustworthy journalism and to campaign for greater media literacy to support public understanding of and rebuild trust in quality journalism.  Oxford and District Branch  SOC recommends that the following amendment puts motion 128 in order. Line 7: delete “calls on” insert “instructs”  Oxford and District Branch  SOC recommends that the following amendment puts motion 128 in order. Line 7, after \"DM\", delete \"calls on\", insert \"ins...")
