      (text "127 This DM notes the Assisted Dying for Terminally Ill Adults Bill is now passing through the Parliamentary process, with the possibility of it becoming law as early as by the end of this year (2025). This DM understands the arguments for and against the Bill, with those for arguing for the right of terminally ill adults having their right to a pain-free death with dignity, and those against concerned over assisted dying being normalised in an era of health and social care austerity where terminally ill individuals may feel pressurised to release their loved ones from financial burden, while at the same time the Bill distracts attention away from the urgent need for improved palliative and hospice end-of-life care.  DM notes that some media organisations have already taken a partisan position, either championing or opposing the Bill. DM is therefore concerned for individual members working for such media organisations being forced by their employers to produce material to which they h...")
