      (id "imp-0772")
      (date "2025-06-05T17:23:08")
      (text "This DM welcomes the decision by the Independent Press Standards Organisation (IPSO) not to uphold a complaint against the Nottingham Post by Nottinghamshire Police.  The newspaper printed details from a 'non disclosure' police briefing about the fatal stabbings of three people in Nottingham in June 2023.  Its editor argued the 'non disclosure' briefing was an unprecedented attempt by the police to prevent reporting information vital to the public's understanding of the case, and crucially the interactions between the police, local mental health services and the attacker months before the killings.  This DM agrees with the editor Natalie Fahy's concern that \"we increasingly find that various institutions try to curtail our freedoms as an independent press, and it's important to take a stand when any of them go too far.\" This DM believes if journalists and media outlets are prevented from reporting information in the public interest, the public suffers.  This DM instructs the NEC to o...")
      (truncated #t))
    (comment
      (id "imp-0773")
      (date "2025-06-05T17:22:12")
      (text "79 Selected motion covering motion 80. Tabling body of covered motion should, where necessary, resubmit as an amendment to the covering motion. Amendments from other tabling bodies should also be made to the selected motion only.  This Delegate Meeting regrets the failure of the UK and Scottish governments to live up to their commitments to produce legislation designed to eradicate egregious, wilful and self-serving recourse by rich, often corrupt individuals to SLAPPs (Strategic Lawsuits to Prevent Public Participation). These suits serve to harass, intimidate and silence journalists and to curtail free speech and fair comment.  That failure has been mirrored in the Republic of Ireland.  DM notes that prominent Labour MPs, now members of the Cabinet such as Foreign Secretary David Lammy, joined with the then Conservative government in fully backing the private member's bill introduced by (former) Labour MP Wayne David but that this bill, already at committee stage, fell when the July ...")
      (truncated #t))
